{"strongs": "H0657", "word": "אָ֑פֶס אֶ֫פֶס", "translit": "e.phes", "root": "אפס", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "ceasing", "definition": "אָ֑פֶס אֶ֫פֶס noun masculine properly ceasing , hence 1. end, extremity , only in the poetic phrase אַפְסֵי אֶרֶץ ( Ps 59:14 הארץ ׳ א ) ends, extreme limits , of the earth, used especially hyperbolically: Deut 33:17 ; 1Sam 2:10 ; Mic 5:3 ; Jer 16:19 ; Ps 2:8 ; Ps 59:14 ; Ps 72:8 (= Zech 9:10 ); + כָּלֿ Isa 45:22 ; Isa 52:10 b (= Ps 98:3 b) Ps 22:28 ; Ps 67:8 ; Prov 30:4 . 2. Expressing non-existence : \\ \\ a. as substantive. (mostly a rare poetic synonym of אַיִן ): Isa 34:12 and all his princes יִהְיוּ אָ֑פֶס shall become nought , ( Isa 41:29 ; Isa 41:12 יִהְיוּ כְאַיִן וּכְאֶפֶס ; Isa 40:17 מֵאֶפֶס וָתֹהוּ (|| כְּאַיִן ) as made of nought and worthlessness are they accounted by him, Isa 41:24 (read פָּעָלְכָם מֵאָ֑פֶס , || מֵאַיִן see אֶפַע ); Isa 52:4 and Asshur oppressed him בְּאֶפֶס for nought. \\ \\ b. as particle of negation, prop. cessation of . . ! (compare אֵין ֗֗֗ nought of ...), very rare in prose ( 2Sam 9:3 ), chiefly a poetic synonym of ׃אֵין Isa 5:8 עַד אֶפֶס מָקוֺם till there is an end of place = till there is no place (compare עַָד אֵין Ps 40:13 ), Amos 6:10 (compare אָֽיִן Judg 4:20 ), Deut 32:36 (hence, in prose, 2Kgs 14:26 ), Isa 45:6 (compare אָין Isa 43:11 ) v Isa 43:14 ; Isa 46:9 ; Isa 54:15 אֲנִי וְאַפְסִי עוֺד Zeph 2:15 ; Isa 47:8 ; Isa 47:10 is probably to be rendered, 'I am, and there is none besides ' (so Ges Ew Di etc.), the י being 'paragogic' as in זוּלָתי etc. ( Ges «GKC:90»§ 90 , 3 a Ew § 211 b ), compare וְאֵין עוֺד Isa 45:5 ; Isa 45:6 ; Isa 45:18 ; Isa 45:21 but according to De the י is suffix of 1 singular 'I am, and I am nought besides' (i.e. and I am nought besides my all-sufficient self). — בְּאֶפֶס (like בְּאֵין , q. v.) without : Prov 14:28 ; Prov 26:20 ; Job 7:6 ; Dan 8:25 . \\ \\ c. as adverb of limitation: \\ \\ \\ ( a ) only : Num 22:35 (compare אַח v Num 22:20 ) Num 23:13 . \\ \\ \\ ( b ) אֶפֶס כִּי save that, howbeit (qualifying a preceding statement): Num 13:28 ; Deut 1:5 ; Judg 4:9 ; Amos 9:8 (+ 1Sam 1:5 ᵐ5 We Sta Dr ). So אֶפֶס alone 2Sam 12:14 (the following כִּי signifying because ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB673')\">BDB673</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H657')\">H657</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB672')\">BDB672</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB674')\">BDB674</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>אָ֑פֶס אֶ֫פֶס</bdbheb> <b>noun masculine</b> properly <highlightword>ceasing</highlightword>, hence <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> <highlightword>end, extremity</highlightword>, only in the poetic phrase <bdbheb>אַפְסֵי</bdbheb> <bdbheb>אֶרֶץ</bdbheb> (<ref ref=\"Ps 59:14\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"59\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"59\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(19,59,14)\">Ps 59:14</ref> <bdbheb>הארץ</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>א</bdbheb>) <highlight>ends, extreme limits</highlight>, of the earth, used especially hyperbolically: <ref ref=\"Deut 33:17\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"33\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"33\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(5,33,17)\">Deut 33:17</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Sam 2:10\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(9,2,10)\">1Sam 2:10</ref>; <ref ref=\"Mic 5:3\" b=\"33\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(33,5,3)\">Mic 5:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 16:19\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(24,16,19)\">Jer 16:19</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 2:8\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(19,2,8)\">Ps 2:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 59:14\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"59\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"59\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(19,59,14)\">Ps 59:14</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 72:8\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"72\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"72\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(19,72,8)\">Ps 72:8</ref> (= <ref ref=\"Zech 9:10\" b=\"38\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(38,9,10)\">Zech 9:10</ref>); + <bdbheb>כָּלֿ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 45:22\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"45\" vBegin=\"22\" cEnd=\"45\" vEnd=\"22\" onclick=\"bcv(23,45,22)\">Isa 45:22</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 52:10\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"52\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"52\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(23,52,10)\">Isa 52:10</ref>b (= <ref ref=\"Ps 98:3\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"98\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"98\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(19,98,3)\">Ps 98:3</ref>b) <ref ref=\"Ps 22:28\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"28\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"28\" onclick=\"bcv(19,22,28)\">Ps 22:28</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 67:8\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"67\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"67\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(19,67,8)\">Ps 67:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Prov 30:4\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"30\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"30\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(20,30,4)\">Prov 30:4</ref>.</p></div><div class=\"section\"><p></div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> Expressing <highlightword>non-existence</highlightword>: <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>a.</b> as substantive. (mostly a rare poetic synonym of <bdbheb>אַיִן</bdbheb>): <ref ref=\"Isa 34:12\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"34\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"34\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(23,34,12)\">Isa 34:12</ref> and all his princes <bdbheb>יִהְיוּ אָ֑פֶס</bdbheb> shall become <highlight>nought</highlight>, (<ref ref=\"Isa 41:29\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"41\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(23,41,29)\">Isa 41:29</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 41:12\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"41\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(23,41,12)\">Isa 41:12</ref> <bdbheb>יִהְיוּ כְאַיִן וּכְאֶפֶס</bdbheb>; <ref ref=\"Isa 40:17\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"40\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"40\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(23,40,17)\">Isa 40:17</ref> <bdbheb>מֵאֶפֶס וָתֹהוּ</bdbheb> (|| <bdbheb>כְּאַיִן</bdbheb>) as made of <highlight>nought</highlight> and worthlessness are they accounted by him, <ref ref=\"Isa 41:24\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"41\" vBegin=\"24\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"24\" onclick=\"bcv(23,41,24)\">Isa 41:24</ref> (read<bdbheb>פָּעָלְכָם</bdbheb> <bdbheb>מֵאָ֑פֶס</bdbheb>, || <bdbheb>מֵאַיִן</bdbheb> see  <bdbheb><reflink>אֶפַע</reflink></bdbheb>); <ref ref=\"Isa 52:4\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"52\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"52\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(23,52,4)\">Isa 52:4</ref> and Asshur oppressed him <bdbheb>בְּאֶפֶס</bdbheb> <highlight>for nought.</highlight> <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>b.</b> as particle of negation, prop. <highlight>cessation of</highlight>. . ! (compare <bdbheb>אֵין ֗֗֗ </bdbheb> <highlight>nought of</highlight>...), very rare in prose (<ref ref=\"2Sam 9:3\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(10,9,3)\">2Sam 9:3</ref>), chiefly a poetic synonym of <bdbheb>׃אֵין</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 5:8\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(23,5,8)\">Isa 5:8</ref> <bdbheb>עַד אֶפֶס מָקוֺם</bdbheb> till there is <highlight>an end of</highlight> place = till there is <highlight>no</highlight> place (compare <bdbheb>עַָד אֵין</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 40:13\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"40\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"40\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(19,40,13)\">Ps 40:13</ref>), <ref ref=\"Amos 6:10\" b=\"30\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(30,6,10)\">Amos 6:10</ref> (compare <bdbheb>אָֽיִן</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Judg 4:20\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(7,4,20)\">Judg 4:20</ref>), <ref ref=\"Deut 32:36\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"36\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"36\" onclick=\"bcv(5,32,36)\">Deut 32:36</ref> (hence, in prose, <ref ref=\"2Kgs 14:26\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"26\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(12,14,26)\">2Kgs 14:26</ref>), <ref ref=\"Isa 45:6\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"45\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"45\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(23,45,6)\">Isa 45:6</ref> (compare <bdbheb>אָין</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 43:11\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"43\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"43\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(23,43,11)\">Isa 43:11</ref>) v<ref ref=\"Isa 43:14\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"43\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"43\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(23,43,14)\">Isa 43:14</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 46:9\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"46\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"46\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(23,46,9)\">Isa 46:9</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 54:15\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"54\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"54\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(23,54,15)\">Isa 54:15</ref> <bdbheb>אֲנִי וְאַפְסִי עוֺד</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Zeph 2:15\" b=\"36\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(36,2,15)\">Zeph 2:15</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 47:8\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"47\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"47\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(23,47,8)\">Isa 47:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 47:10\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"47\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"47\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(23,47,10)\">Isa 47:10</ref> is probably to be rendered, 'I am, and <highlight>there is none besides</highlight>' (so <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ges')\">Ges</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ew')\">Ew</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Di')\">Di</lookup> etc.), the <bdbheb>י</bdbheb> being 'paragogic' as in <bdbheb>זוּלָתי</bdbheb> etc. (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ges')\">Ges</lookup><sup>«GKC:90»§ 90</sup>, 3 a <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ew')\">Ew<sup>§ 211 b</sup></lookup>), compare <bdbheb>וְאֵין עוֺד</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 45:5\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"45\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"45\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(23,45,5)\">Isa 45:5</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 45:6\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"45\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"45\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(23,45,6)\">Isa 45:6</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 45:18\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"45\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"45\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(23,45,18)\">Isa 45:18</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 45:21\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"45\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"45\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(23,45,21)\">Isa 45:21</ref> but according to <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('De')\">De</lookup> the <bdbheb>י</bdbheb> is suffix of 1 singular 'I am, and <highlight>I am nought</highlight> besides' (i.e. and I am nought besides my all-sufficient self). — <bdbheb>בְּאֶפֶס</bdbheb> (like <bdbheb>בְּאֵין</bdbheb>, q. v.) <highlight>without</highlight>: <ref ref=\"Prov 14:28\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"28\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"28\" onclick=\"bcv(20,14,28)\">Prov 14:28</ref>; <ref ref=\"Prov 26:20\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"26\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"26\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(20,26,20)\">Prov 26:20</ref>; <ref ref=\"Job 7:6\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(18,7,6)\">Job 7:6</ref>; <ref ref=\"Dan 8:25\" b=\"27\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(27,8,25)\">Dan 8:25</ref>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>c.</b> as adverb of limitation: <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;\\&emsp;(<highlight>a</highlight>) <highlight>only</highlight>: <ref ref=\"Num 22:35\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"35\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"35\" onclick=\"bcv(4,22,35)\">Num 22:35</ref> (compare <bdbheb>אַח</bdbheb> v<ref ref=\"Num 22:20\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(4,22,20)\">Num 22:20</ref>) <ref ref=\"Num 23:13\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(4,23,13)\">Num 23:13</ref>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;\\&emsp;(<highlight>b</highlight>) <bdbheb>אֶפֶס כִּי</bdbheb> <highlight>save that, howbeit</highlight> (qualifying a preceding statement): <ref ref=\"Num 13:28\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"28\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"28\" onclick=\"bcv(4,13,28)\">Num 13:28</ref>; <ref ref=\"Deut 1:5\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(5,1,5)\">Deut 1:5</ref>; <ref ref=\"Judg 4:9\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(7,4,9)\">Judg 4:9</ref>; <ref ref=\"Amos 9:8\" b=\"30\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(30,9,8)\">Amos 9:8</ref> (+ <ref ref=\"1Sam 1:5\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(9,1,5)\">1Sam 1:5</ref> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('We')\">We</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sta')\">Sta</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Dr')\">Dr</lookup>). So <bdbheb>אֶפֶס</bdbheb> alone <ref ref=\"2Sam 12:14\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(10,12,14)\">2Sam 12:14</ref> (the following <bdbheb>כִּי</bdbheb> signifying <highlight>because</highlight>). </p></div><hr>", "references": [{"raw": "Ps 59:14", "book": "PSA", "chapter": 59, "verse": 14}, {"raw": "Deut 33:17", "book": "DEU", "chapter": 33, "verse": 17}, {"raw": "1Sam 2:10", "book": "1SA", "chapter": 2, "verse": 10}, {"raw": "Mic 5:3", "book": "MIC", "chapter": 5, "verse": 3}, {"raw": "Jer 16:19", "book": "JER", "chapter": 16, "verse": 19}, {"raw": "Ps 2:8", "book": "PSA", "chapter": 2, "verse": 8}, {"raw": "Ps 72:8", "book": "PSA", "chapter": 72, "verse": 8}, {"raw": "Zech 9:10", "book": "ZEC", "chapter": 9, "verse": 10}, {"raw": "Isa 45:22", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 45, "verse": 22}, {"raw": "Isa 52:10", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 52, "verse": 10}, {"raw": "Ps 98:3", "book": "PSA", "chapter": 98, "verse": 3}, {"raw": "Ps 22:28", "book": "PSA", "chapter": 22, "verse": 28}, {"raw": "Ps 67:8", "book": "PSA", "chapter": 67, "verse": 8}, {"raw": "Prov 30:4", "book": "PRO", "chapter": 30, "verse": 4}, {"raw": "Isa 34:12", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 34, "verse": 12}, {"raw": "Isa 41:29", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 41, "verse": 29}, {"raw": "Isa 41:12", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 41, "verse": 12}, {"raw": "Isa 40:17", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 40, "verse": 17}, {"raw": "Isa 41:24", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 41, "verse": 24}, {"raw": "Isa 52:4", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 52, "verse": 4}, {"raw": "2Sam 9:3", "book": "2SA", "chapter": 9, "verse": 3}, {"raw": "Isa 5:8", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 5, "verse": 8}, {"raw": "Ps 40:13", "book": "PSA", "chapter": 40, "verse": 13}, {"raw": "Amos 6:10", "book": "AMO", "chapter": 6, "verse": 10}, {"raw": "Judg 4:20", "book": "JDG", "chapter": 4, "verse": 20}, {"raw": "Deut 32:36", "book": "DEU", "chapter": 32, "verse": 36}, {"raw": "2Kgs 14:26", "book": "2KI", "chapter": 1